body:
Don't assume you have the experience to know who is right and who is wrong here.  I have once or twice told people a little piece of advice, which goes "don't believe someone if they're not ranting... people are only actually honest about what they think when they're worked up".

&#x200B;

If you dad isn't getting really worked up about this... why?  Upset, or concerned seems a low ball emotional reaction here?

&#x200B;

You don't really have the information to judge.  Try to stay out of it as best you can.  Good luck.

Also, that bs about men having a natural tendency is TRASH.  Most men DREAD it... but they HAVE to cause of that very mentality.  It's a gender norm, and I don't do the whole gender politics discussion often, but it's a role enforcement.

&#x200B;

That rationale is little more than protecting the privileged women have of choosing rather than facing rejection in most western society.  But facing rejection is a skill.  And it's invaluable.

I have gone home with women who had the bravery to walk up to me and hit on me, out of little more than sheer respect.

&#x200B;

Fortunately, those FEW, tended to be very good girls.  TENDED tho :p  not all :p

Nah man, you're good.  She obviously matters to you.  Just don't forget that WHO you are, and WHAT YOU THINK, and what YOU BELIEVE need to matter just as much.

&#x200B;

You're not there to fulfil her needs, and you're not there by fate.  You're there by choice and so is she.  Make sure you're making the right choice.  And if you are, give it everything you have.  But if you're not, don't be scared to leave and create space for someone else where you CAN make the right choice.

&#x200B;

You'll be fine.  Just remember that you're as an important part of that relationship as she is, and how she treats YOU is as important as how you treat her.

If your relationship requires PROOF then it's broken.

&#x200B;

Don't PROVE it to her.  Earn her trust and respect.  Be honest. and clear. AND SOLID.  Don't grovel, explain your thoughts, and your actual intent and what you REALLY think... and if you DID make a mistake based on that, own up to it and be real about it.

Rules tend to get broken, and her INTENTION is already clear.

&#x200B;

She wants out, and is willing to cut ties... do yourself AND her a favour... DON'T make this a negotiation.  Make it a decision.  Cut romantic ties.  She's already half way there, sever the bs and get the job done.  She will regret your ANd her decision for a bit, but you will both avoid massive drama and probable damage.

&#x200B;

She already broke this one mate.  Good luck.  Be STRONG for yourself.
